      "rev_n_16_66427d_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_16_66427d_1",
        "node_id": "n_16_66427d",
        "thought_text": "I understand the issue with the current implementation. The main problem is that it's not considering all possible words to add to the dictionary, and it's not updating the dictionary correctly when checking for the best word to add. Let's refine our approach by considering words that differ by one letter from any word in the dictionary, not just the start word. This would potentially find better solutions by exploring more of the word space and considering words that might be closer to the end word.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8056519455972941595",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_16_66427d_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_5816aa712d",
        "created_at": 1794535080.7659507
      },
      "rev_n_17_7edffb_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_17_7edffb_1",
        "node_id": "n_17_7edffb",
        "thought_text": "For the Word Ladder problem with dictionary addition, the current approach of checking all possible words to add and then performing BFS for each addition is inefficient and prone to errors. A more effective strategy would be to first perform a BFS without adding any new words, and then, if no path is found, consider adding words that connect the start and end words in the existing graph. This approach would be more efficient and less likely to miss optimal solutions.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8056519455972941595",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_17_7edffb_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_3e13bb6bcd",
        "created_at": 1794535185.4438837
